        "original_id": "752b61a2-1abf-5388-b089-d86c2f529533",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: ValuJet Airlines\n- People: Candalyn \"Candi\" Kubeck\n- Events: ValuJet Flight 592 crash\n- Places: Miami, Everglades, Clayton County, Georgia, Eastern United States, Canada\n- Products: McDonnell-Douglas DC-9\n\nFacts:\n- ValuJet Airlines was an American low-cost carrier headquartered in unincorporated Clayton County, Georgia, and it operated scheduled domestic and international flights in the Eastern United States and Canada during the 1990s.\n- Candalyn \"Candi\" Kubeck was born on May 10, 1961.\n- On May 11, 1996, Candalyn \"Candi\" Kubeck died as the captain of ValuJet Flight 592.\n- On May 11, 1996, a ValuJet Airlines McDonnell-Douglas DC-9 operating ValuJet Flight 592 crashed into the Everglades about 11 minutes after takeoff from Miami.\n- The ValuJet Flight 592 crash was caused by a fire in the cargo compartment that resulted from improperly stored cargo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
